From 0cbbc98ed684c4c5c1a561bcd42f335a53e152d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:12:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban-sync): timing analyzer fails closed on
 prefix, schema and provenance

Review corrections for 4f388d7586a (REVIEW.md F1 blocking, F2-F6 non-blocking).

- F1 analyzer: records before the first start (junk, orphans, a capture whose start is
  missing) are kept as their own leading capture and fail as no_start_marker instead of
  being dropped; validate adds schema_mismatch, unknown_event, field_not_allowed (the
  writer's own _allowed), and identity_unverified (code_src != boot, no code, or
  disk_moved). A record missing a needed field yields malformed_record, never a crash.
- F2 writer: code identity is resolved before the fd is opened (any exception leaves the
  capture unverified), and the fd is closed if start setup fails before the capture owns it.
- F4/F3/F5 docs: stop happens at the first loop boundary after the bound (no hard timer,
  overrun up to one round plus one wait); select holds the diag lock across
  SyncWork.select while armed (feed callback wait shows in chg.lk); rotation keeps only
  one .1, so archive a capture before arming the next.
- F6: unserviced counts changes only; boards past PEND_MAX are unserviced_boards_truncated.

The real-loop test now injects a boot identity: a test process has none, and the analyzer
correctly reports that as identity_unverified.

Proof: 16 new tests RED on the HEAD source, GREEN 187 passed / 0 failed across timing,
timing_loop, machine_metrics, config_runtime_keys, kanban_sync_client; scripts/check ok.
